{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/undirectedincidencelist"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedIncidenceList"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedIncidenceList"}],"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs23UndirectedIncidenceListV","title":"UndirectedIncidenceList","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList.swift#L30","fileName":"UndirectedIncidenceList.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected hypergraph stored as an incidence list: a row per hyperedge of its members and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row per vertex of its memberships. The undirected counterpart of ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", named as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is. (","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the bit-matrix representation, is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undirected one of its pair, because “oriented incidence matrix” is the established name of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other.)","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices are any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values, kept in an ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrderedSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose element ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the vertices listed first, then new members by first appearance, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assigns them. A hyperedge is a set of vertices of any size, the empty set included; repeated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedges are kept, each at its own position ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<hyperedgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a member listed twice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is stored once. Members are stored in vertex-index order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is compressed sparse rows: the members of every hyperedge in one array, and for every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex its incidence numbers and, beside them, its hyperedge positions, in rows of shared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pools. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArraySlice<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read without hashing, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex-space read hashes its vertex once; index-space reads and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hash none."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hyperedges can be appended but not removed (removal, and with it a decision on positions, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left for later). Equality ignores the order of the vertices and of the hyperedges."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps from the vertices and the hyperedges to values can be attached ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"): a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex map is read by vertex index or by vertex, an edge map by hyperedge position."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init()","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(hyperedges:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(vertices:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/init(vertices:hyperedges:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/degree(checked:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceList\/incidentHyperedges(checked:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/UndirectedIncidenceLi